            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0718" n="594" xml:id="pg594"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2170c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-15T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1921—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>405. Following is the substance of a memorandum handed yesterday to the Chinese
                    Minister at Washington. Inform Embassy, Paris, by mail.</p>
                <p>[Here follows summary of memorandum to the Chinese Legation printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Inform Foreign Office and suggest that the British Minister at Peking be
                    instructed to support this view with the Chinese Government. The American
                    representatives at Peking and Tokyo are being instructed to advise their British
                    colleagues.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
